# Copy to local.personal-data (never committed) and list what is personal to
# you: scripts/check-personal-data reports every match. One Python regular
# expression per line; "#" starts a comment; a line starting with "!" is an
# allow pattern (a finding whose text or line matches it is dropped).
# The phone's address and MAC in local.env are added automatically.

# Machines and shares on your network: host names, ssh aliases, NAS mounts
(?i)\bmy-desktop\b
(?i)/mnt/my-nas\b
# Your accounts and names
(?i)\bmy-login-name\b
# The phone: its serial number, your WiFi networks' names
\bSERIAL0123\b
\bMyHomeWiFi\b

# Allowed: your copyright line is your choice
!^Copyright \(c\) \d{4} My Name$
